/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 424 0 R
/E (Zhao et al. \(2024\), Computer Methods in Applied Mechanics and Engineering. This work used a matrix-free GPU method to speed up large topology optimization problems. Their approach reduces the storage and computational cost of repeated mechanical simulations. This supports our plan for GPU acceleration, although their method was tested on composite structures rather than biodegradable implants.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [200 0 R 11]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Existing studies cover corrosion, mechanical performance, bone remodeling, topology optimization, and GPU computing separately. Our project aims to connect these parts in one framework for designing biodegradable implants that remain mechanically safe throughout healing.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
